# Module 40 – HI-TECH College AI Administration, Usage & Governance

This module introduces the central AI control centre for the college. The Super Admin can manage AI availability, approved models, usage limits, knowledge indexing, prompt versions and audit records.

The design separates institution-wide AI governance from individual chatbot conversations. API credentials remain on the server, while administrators only see provider configuration status—not secret values.

The module includes:

1. AI provider configuration and health checks.
2. Global emergency disable switch.
3. Institution-specific AI settings.
4. Monthly usage and token accounting.
5. Usage quotas and role-based limits.
6. Versioned prompt templates.
7. Knowledge indexing status.
8. AI governance audit logs.

## 1. Database schema

Add the following models and enums to `apps/api/prisma/schema.prisma`. The `ChatbotAIConfiguration` model from Module 39 should be extended rather than duplicated.

```

enum AIProviderStatus {
  ACTIVE
  DISABLED
  DEGRADED
}

enum AIAuditAction {
  CONFIG_UPDATED
  AI_ENABLED
  AI_DISABLED
  EMERGENCY_DISABLED
  PROVIDER_CHECKED
  PROMPT_CREATED
  PROMPT_PUBLISHED
  PROMPT_ARCHIVED
  QUOTA_UPDATED
  INDEXING_REQUESTED
}

enum AIPromptStatus {
  DRAFT
  PUBLISHED
  ARCHIVED
}

model AIProviderConfiguration {
  id             String           @id @default(uuid())
  institutionId  String
